 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-nagata-maximal-isomorphism-open"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "A union of opens is open. On pairwise intersections, the inverses of the\nrestricted morphisms agree because an inverse to a fixed morphism is unique;\nhence the local inverses glue to an inverse over the union. If an open\n$W$ has the property that $q^{-1}(W)\\to W$ is an isomorphism, then $W$ is\none of the opens in the defining union, and therefore $W\\subseteq \\operatorname{IsoOpen}(q)$; this is the maximality assertion.",
   "uses": [],
   "elementary": null
  }
 ],
